# Build-time configuration for the academy site.
#
# This file is committed on purpose, and everything in it is public. Vite
# inlines every VITE_-prefixed value into the JavaScript it emits, so anything
# here is readable by anyone who opens the bundle — committing it changes
# nothing about who can see it, and it is what lets the GitHub Pages build
# produce a working site without a secret store.
#
# Never put a credential here. A Google *client secret*, an API key, a database
# URL: none of those belong in a VITE_ variable at all, because the browser
# would receive them. Use `.env.local` (git-ignored) for anything you would not
# publish, and the server's own environment for real secrets.

# Google OAuth client ID for Sign in with Google. Public by design — it
# identifies the application, and Google enforces which origins may use it.
#
# Sign-in only works from an origin listed under "Authorized JavaScript origins"
# for this client in the Google Cloud console; anywhere else Google refuses with
# origin_mismatch. Leave this empty and the sign-in button is not rendered at all.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=1028322175067-264k5f61vc0o1jpfjkvt0ssmctio5m7s.apps.googleusercontent.com
